"y":2309,"w":155,"h":40},{"text":"His:","x":1999,"y":2446,"w":60,"h":29},{"text":"She/","x":1999,"y":2546,"w":74,"h":29},{"text":"Her:","x":1999,"y":2589,"w":65,"h":29},{"text":"They/","x":1998,"y":2688,"w":92,"h":37},{"text":"Them: Ü","x":1997,"y":2725,"w":155,"h":39},{"text":"C nouv","x":1257,"y":2746,"w":252,"h":54},{"text":"is side only) for alternate signers attached to this form and the argument.","x":808,"y":2835,"w":1267,"h":39}]},{"page":7,"width":2448,"height":3168,"lines":[{"text":"Rebuttal to Argument Against the San Mateo Sales Tax Measure","x":272,"y":286,"w":1358,"h":42},{"text":"We agree on one thing: every tax dollar must be spent responsibly. However, fiscal","x":268,"y":403,"w":1725,"h":44},{"text":"responsibility also means confronting reality and not allowing the services we depend on to","x":270,"y":461,"w":1859,"h":46},{"text":"deteriorate.","x":269,"y":520,"w":233,"h":34},{"text":"Measure H asks for an additional 1/4$ to protect the basics that keep San Mateo safe and","x":270,"y":637,"w":1780,"h":45},{"text":"strong: police and fire protection, paramedics and 911 response, safer streets and pothole","x":269,"y":696,"w":1843,"h":45},{"text":"repair, clean parks and other essential city services.","x":269,"y":754,"w":1053,"h":44},{"text":"Opponents argue that approximately $7 million won't eliminate the projected deficit, which","x":268,"y":869,"w":1857,"h":48},{"text":"is now $18.2 million. But rejecting $7 million because it doesn't solve every problem means","x":269,"y":926,"w":1857,"h":49},{"text":"the city will have to make more significant cuts that affect our everyday lives. Measure H is","x":266,"y":989,"w":1837,"h":45},{"text":"about the people who coach your child's Little League team, who make Music in the Park","x":267,"y":1048,"w":1807,"h":44},{"text":"happen, who respond to the 17-year-old's cardiac arrest fast enough to save their life and","x":268,"y":1106,"w":1812,"h":45},{"text":"so much more.","x":266,"y":1166,"w":302,"h":33},{"text":"We should demand efficiency and accountability City Hall. Yet efficiency alone doesn't fill","x":264,"y":1282,"w":1832,"h":45},{"text":"potholes, answer 91 1 calls, or ensure firefighters and paramedics are there when our","x":268,"y":1341,"w":1728,"h":44},{"text":"families need them.","x":265,"y":1400,"w":401,"h":33},{"text":"We should insist on accountability and protect essential services. An oversight committee","x":264,"y":1518,"w":1842,"h":45},{"text":"will continue reviewing how funds are allocated and spent, providing transparency and","x":264,"y":1576,"w":1760,"h":46},{"text":"public accountability.","x":266,"y":1635,"w":437,"h":42},{"text":"And let's be clear: this measure will not increase the cost of groceries or prescription","x":264,"y":1752,"w":1802,"h":46},{"text":"medications, which are exempt from sales tax.","x":266,"y":1812,"w":962,"h":41},{"text":"Measure H is a practical investment in the city we all call home—while demanding","x":266,"y":1928,"w":1672,"h":46},{"text":"responsible stewardship of every dollar.","x":266,"y":1987,"w":807,"h":42},{"text":"Vote YES on Measure H for a safe, strong, and fiscally responsible San Mateo.","x":263,"y":2105,"w":1656,"h":44},{"text":"FILED","x":751,"y":2329,"w":93,"h":32},{"text":"OFFICE OF THE CHIEF ELECTIONS OFFICER","x":436,"y":2376,"w":725,"h":37},{"text":"SAN MATEO CCUNIY","x":626,"y":2427,"w":347,"h":35},{"text":"13","x":2279,"y":694,"w":48,"h":46},{"text":"2","x":2294,"y":864,"w":32,"h":46},{"text":"2","x":2283,"y":1637,"w":37,"h":35},{"text":"AUG 1 8 2026","x":668,"y":2539,"w":262,"h":48},{"text":"TIONS OFFICER","x":906,"y":2656,"w":260,"h":33},{"text":"MARK C","x":436,"y":2660,"w":129,"h":34},{"text":"BY:","x":437,"y":2733,"w":50,"h":32}]},{"page":8,"width":2448,"height":3168,"lines":[{"text":"Rebuttal to Argument Against the San Mateo Sales Tax Measure","x":319,"y":353,"w":1297,"h":42},{"text":"We agree on one thing: every tax dollar must be spent responsibly. However, fiscal","x":315,"